src/vr/ArmRoll.cpp (the roll-aware arm IK of the VR body, #304) ports the rules of the limb solver
of RENIK, https://github.com/V-Sekai/renik at commit 1d4028a65b21a05c86714baa48a459a3a7aaaeca
(renik/renik_limb.h, renik.cpp: solve_trig_ik_redux and the arm defaults): how the hand's roll is
shared between the forearm and the upper arm (lower_limb_twist, upper_limb_twist), how it steers the
joint (target_rotation_influence), and the inflection point with its overflow hysteresis
(twist_inflection_point_offset, twist_overflow, overflow_state). RENIK distributes those files
under the MIT License; its notices are reproduced below. Nothing of RENIK is compiled into this
tree: the C++ here is our own writing of the rules against this engine's skeleton (bend-plane frames
from the model's rest pose, a swing-twist split), distributed under the GPLv3+ like the rest of the
tree.

